# dvcom

```
compress files from your terminal. no cloud. no uploads. your machine only.
```

## Install

```bash
pip install dvcom
```

That's it.

> Also needs Ghostscript + ImageMagick:
> ```bash
> # mac
> brew install ghostscript imagemagick
>
> # linux
> sudo apt install ghostscript imagemagick
>
> # windows
> # download installers from ghostscript.com and imagemagick.org
> ```

---

## Usage

```bash
dvcom file.pdf                    # compress to -40% (default)
dvcom file.pdf 2MB                # compress to target 2 MB
dvcom photo.jpg 500KB             # compress image to 500 KB
dvcom *.pdf 1MB                   # batch compress all PDFs
dvcom file.pdf 2MB -o ~/Desktop   # save to Desktop
dvcom photo.jpg 300KB -o out/small.jpg   # custom output filename
dvcom file.pdf -v                 # verbose: show compression steps
```

---

## Why

- **Slow internet?** Compress before you send. Entirely offline.
- **Private files?** Nothing leaves your machine. Ever.
- **Nerdy?** It uses Ghostscript's 3-strategy cascade + binary search to hit your target size.

---

## How it works

For PDFs, tries 3 strategies in order:
1. Font/stream optimisation (lossless)
2. qpdf repack (if installed)
3. DPI binary search (hits target size)

For images, binary searches the best quality level that fits your target.

